# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository. Without this, whether a
# commit lands as LF or CRLF depends on each machine's core.autocrlf, which is
# how a whitespace-only diff of an entire file happens.
#
# eol=crlf pins the working copy too, rather than leaving it to core.autocrlf:
# this is a Windows-only app, and pinning it means a checkout is identical on
# every machine and there is no "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on commit.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Shell scripts must keep LF even on Windows: CRLF breaks the shebang line and
# gives "bad interpreter" under Git Bash, WSL and CI containers.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binaries git must never touch. None are tracked today; these are here so
# adding a tray icon or a screenshot cannot corrupt it through normalisation.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.exe binary
